ness","usage":{"input_tokens":17123,"output_tokens":1118,"requests":2}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how the per-item allow_unharnessed_subprocess marker maps to per-call-site AST hazards (e.g. suppression granularity: file-level vs. within the marked function's line span) and how multi-spawn / multi-test files and helper-defined spawns are resolved.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The opt-out is @pytest.mark.allow_unharnessed_subprocess(\"<reason>\")'","Detection is 'AST ... resolve ast.Call sites' — hazards are line-keyed, not item-keyed","Precedent _live_jira_confinement.py keys on item markers (get_closest_marker) where 1 mark == 1 item; here the item↔call-site relation is many-to-many"],"finding":"The opt-out is a per-item marker (@pytest.mark.allow_unharnessed_subprocess on a test function/class) but hazards are AST call sites keyed by file+line; the plan does not specify how a marker on one item suppresses a specific call site, so a file with multiple tests/spawn sites can over-suppress (a marker on one test silences a sibling test's real hazard in the same module) or under-suppress (a hazard in a helper reached from the marked test but defined elsewhere).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9077e14b0dff8801","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — opt-out marker; File impact — the ~26 hazard sites","norm_id":"n5a16fb1a18a6ebf3","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A test module has two test functions each spawning a subprocess; one is legitimately marked, the other is a genuine hazard — an item-level marker cannot distinguish them","A marked test calls a helper (in the same or another module) whose spawn site is the actual hazard"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirm